      "text": "To install PowerContext, you need Python 3.11+, Git, and uv. The latest version, 1.3.0, includes an interactive setup wizard. To run the wizard, use the command: ``powercontext[cli,server]==1.3.0``. The wizard guides you through storage options, memory capabilities, and Agent connections. For Windows, support is experimental. The package also depends on `powercontext[client]`, `langgraph`, `langchain-core`, and `pydantic-settings`. For the `powercontext-langgraph` adapter, install from source with `uv pip install./integrations/langgraph`.\nTo install PowerContext, you need Python 3.11+, Git, and uv. The installation includes an interactive setup wizard where you can choose between Basic memory or Full memory. For Basic memory, explicit saves and recall are available without model APIs, while Full memory requires separate Generation and Embedding API credentials. To connect an Agent, install its CLI. The installation supports macOS and Linux, with Windows support being experimental. Applications can use PowerContext through the async Python client, HTTP API, MCP, or the in-process Core SDK. For the complete development workflow, see the CONTRIBUTING.md file.\nTo install the powercontext package, you can use pip, which is included with modern versions of Python. The PyPI documentation advises that installing packages from PyPI involves running third-party code, which carries inherent security risks. It recommends reading the package security guide before installation. The powercontext package description on PyPI does not provide specific installation requirements beyond the use of pip. To install, you can use the command `pip install powercontext`.\n4 days ago \u00b7 PowerContext is an open-source context service for AI agents. It keeps the durable part of your work \u2014 decisions, constraints, evidence, progress \u2014 outside any single conversation, so the next session, the next agent, or the next person can pick up from the current state instead of rereading the transcript.\nPowerContext 1.3.0 includes an interactive setup wizard. You need Python 3.11+, Git, and uv; uv can provision Python when needed. To connect an Agent, also install its CLI. In the wizard, choose Basic memory for explicit saves and recall without model APIs; Full memory requires separate Generation and Embedding API credentials. For a local Server without model APIs, see Install and run. macOS and Linux are supported; Windows support is `experimental`.\n\nChoose the path that matches your goal: [..\n### Install and upgrade\n\nAfter the package is published:\n\n```\n\"powercontext[cli,server]==1.3.0\" \" \"\n```\n\nPreserve the extras used by your deployment, such as `code` or `seekdb`. Upgrade Server, clients, and Agent integrations together.\n\nExisting Memory databases require maintenance before the new service starts. Back up the complete database and configuration. Complete any required processing migration first, then use the new CLI and deployment configuration: [...] feat(embedder): zero-config st\nLoopback HTTP is allowed by default; non-loopback HTTP requires explicit consent through the environment variable above or `allow_insecure_http=True` on `PowerContextLangGraphSettings` or `PowerContextScope`. HTTPS certificate validation stays enabled. Common environment settings and endpoint-bound saved consent are described in Connect to a remote Server. The framework adapter does not have a setup installer. [...] From a checkout you can install the local path instead: `uv pip install ./integr\nInstall a Python role ... Use builtin for in-process Python composition, server for the service, client for the Python SDK, or cli for the Server-backed command",
